{
 "id": "lem-trf-smooth-geometrically-normal",
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Smooth schemes over fields are geometrically normal",
 "statement": "Let $k$ be a field and $X$ a scheme with a smooth morphism $X\\to\\operatorname{Spec}(k)$ [def-pc-scheme, def-sbc-smooth-morphisms]. Then $X$ is geometrically normal over $k$: for every field extension $K/k$ [def-pc-field-extension], every local ring of the base change $X_K=X\\times_{\\operatorname{Spec}k}\\operatorname{Spec}K$ [def-pc-base-change] is a normal domain [def-weil-pbc-normal-ring]. In particular $X$ is geometrically reduced over $k$ [def-pc-geometrically-irreducible].",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/stacks-project/varieties.tex",
  "place": "Tag 056T, lemma-smooth-geometrically-normal."
 },
